The main secret is this: patience.

There are large portions of the game where you can get away with just 
hammering the buttons without thinking too much, but that can get you 
killed by bumping into a floating eye <spork>or grey fungus</spork>.

Have a look through your causes of death, and think about what you could 
have done to prevent each one:

* anything, while helpless: Slow down, learn to use the g<dir> movement 
so you don't get into a situation where you accidentally hit a floating 
eye or gelatinous cube.
* starvation: eat everything. If it turns out to be poisonous, make a 
note and don't eat that particular monster next game. There's plenty of 
food in NetHack
* deadly poison: get PR early. (Eat cave spiders, among other things.)
* cockatrice corpse accident: Take good care with them!
* soldier ant: Get good armour and good XL before descending too deep. 
Try on *everything* noncursed, you do find +2 and +3 armour in the dungeon.
* [random monster]: most monsters are trivially easy to run away from. 
If you get killed in combat, it's mostly because you didn't run away 
before your HP reached 0. Engrave E on the ground relentlessly.

Almost all deaths are YASDs - that is, they are almost all completely 
avoidable. You just have to learn to avoid them. NetHack isn't about 
advancing, it's about not dying.


